<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  LOCKED_SEASONS_DECIDE_FIFTEEN_DEGREE_WOBBLE. Owner, by card 2026-10-20: "Every tile swings ~15 C with the
  seasons: what should seasons do?" -> "Remove the swing".

  Alien Worlds transpiles vanilla GenTemperature.SeasonalShiftAmplitudeAt to read the ACTIVE planet type's
  seasonalTempVariationCurve (FieldPatcher, set in PlanetTypeDef.OnActivate when the curve is non-null). The
  TidallyLocked def ships 0:15 / 1:15 / 2:5, i.e. +-15 C seasons on every tile, opposite sign per hemisphere.
  A tidally locked planet with no axial tilt has none: this flattens the curve to 0 (kept NON-null, so the
  framework still installs it instead of falling back to vanilla's latitude seasons). Each tile then holds its
  painted average all year (daily swing is already off under the lock).

  With Worldbuilder loaded (the full list) this curve is NOT read: Worldbuilder's prefix skips the method body and
  its postfix uses its axial-tilt curve (measured 2026-10-20, audit §8). RM_TidalNoSeasonsPatch (C#, Priority.Last)
  zeroes the amplitude on that backend; this patch covers the standalone one.

  Guarded: FindMod on the tidal-lock mod's name (a top-level MayRequire is ignored), then a Conditional on the
  node, so it is silent when the mod or the field is absent. Takes effect at the next load (activation).
  Design: design/RimMandrake/world_physics_audit_2026-10-20.md §3.
-->
<Patch>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Alien Worlds - Tidally Locked</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
      <xpath>/Defs/AlienWorlds.TidallyLocked.PlanetTypeDef[defName="TidallyLocked"]/seasonalTempVariationCurve</xpath>
      <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
        <xpath>/Defs/AlienWorlds.TidallyLocked.PlanetTypeDef[defName="TidallyLocked"]/seasonalTempVariationCurve</xpath>
        <value>
          <seasonalTempVariationCurve>
            <points>
              <li>0.0, 0</li>
              <li>2.0, 0</li>
            </points>
          </seasonalTempVariationCurve>
        </value>
      </match>
    </match>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
